English
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Why the source is visible. This repository is public only so that its
   continuous-integration tests can run. Public visibility is not a licence.
   No right to use the software is granted by this repository being public,
   by downloading it, or by forking it on GitHub.

2. What is allowed without a licence. You may view the source code on
   GitHub, and GitHub may display and let you fork it as its Terms of Service
   require. Nothing else.

3. What requires written permission. Without a written licence from HCC Lab
   (a signed MD20 licence file issued by HCC Lab counts as one, within its
   stated scope and expiry), you may not:
   (a) install, run or otherwise use the software or any part of it, for any
       purpose, including teaching, research, evaluation and benchmarking;
   (b) copy, modify, translate, adapt or create derivative works;
   (c) distribute, publish, sublicense, sell, rent or lend it, or make it
       available as a service;
   (d) remove, disable or work around the licence check, the provenance
       stamps or any copyright notice;
   (e) use the software, its output, or its source code to train or evaluate
       machine-learning models.

4. Licence files. A licence file is valid only if it carries a valid
   signature made with HCC Lab's private key, is used within its expiry date
   and on the machines it names (if any), and is used by the person it names.
   Licence files are personal and may not be shared.

5. Output. Results you produce with a valid licence may be used in your own
   coursework, theses and publications, with the provenance stamps left in
   place and MD20 acknowledged.

6. Third-party components. Third-party software that MD20 downloads or calls
   (for example OpenMM, AutoDock Vina, RDKit, micromamba) remains under its
   own licence. This licence covers HCC Lab's own code, documentation, data
   and designs in this repository.

7. No warranty. The software is provided "as is", without warranty of any
   kind. HCC Lab is not liable for any damage arising from its use.

8. Termination. Any breach ends every permission immediately. Licence files
   may be revoked.

9. Contact for licences: HCC Lab, National Kaohsiung University of Science and
   Technology, through the repository owner on GitHub (fstcch-cmd).

